From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:28:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 28/30] gunyah: iceland gvm: request the RM-RPC queue in the
 shared memory mode too (pvm51)

pvm51: the boot shim found /hypervisor with doorbells, the shared-memory and the VM-id nodes, but no resource-manager
node, so it could not accept its RAM window. That node comes from the vm-config rm-rpc vdevice, which crosvm only
requested with CROSVM_GVM_ACCEPT=1 (the 3D display's GuestAccept). It is now requested whenever the protection type
shares the guest RAM.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 hypervisor/src/gunyah/aarch64.rs | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hypervisor/src/gunyah/aarch64.rs b/hypervisor/src/gunyah/aarch64.rs
index 3b271a5..7abc260 100644
--- a/hypervisor/src/gunyah/aarch64.rs
+++ b/hypervisor/src/gunyah/aarch64.rs
@@ -145,7 +145,13 @@ impl VmAArch64 for GunyahVm {
             bell_node.set_prop("interrupts", &interrupts)?;
         }
 
-        if self.protected && super::gvm_accept::accept_enabled_by_env() {
+        // pvm51: the shared memory mode's boot shim accepts the RAM window over the same RM-RPC queue, so the
+        // node must exist in that mode too (the shim found /hypervisor with doorbells but no RM node: no rm-rpc
+        // vdevice had been requested, because CROSVM_GVM_ACCEPT was only set for the 3D display).
+        if self.protected
+            && (super::gvm_accept::accept_enabled_by_env()
+                || self.hv_cfg.protection_type.shares_guest_ram())
+        {
             // iceland gvm: ask the RM for an RM-RPC msgq pair; it generates
             // /hypervisor/qcom,resource-mgr (compatible "gunyah-resource-manager",
             // reg = <tx_capid rx_capid>) for the guest's MEM_ACCEPT / MEM_RELEASE.
